---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — CG Design & Co."
  description="The terms that apply when you work with CG Design & Co. on a website project."
  pageTitle="Terms & Conditions"
  lastUpdated="24 October 2026"
>
  <h2>Who these terms apply to</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply whenever you ask CG Design &amp; Co. (ABN 25 672 082
    550) to design, build, or maintain a website or related work ("the
    services"). By agreeing to a quote or proposal from us, you accept
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Quotes and pricing</h2>
  <p>
    We give you a fixed, written price before any work begins, based on the
    pages and features you choose. That price won't change once agreed,
    unless you ask us to add extra pages or features partway through — in
    which case we'll agree the extra cost with you first. Figures shown by
    the pricing estimator on this site are indicative until confirmed in
    writing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our project fee covers design and build. Ongoing hosting, maintenance,
    and domain management are separate services, covered below.
  </p>

  <h2>Domain registration and renewal</h2>
  <p>
    If we register a domain name on your behalf as part of your project,
    we cover the cost of that first registration period. After that, the
    domain needs to be renewed each year to stay active.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where we manage a domain's renewal for you, the annual renewal is
    billed to you and may include a standard domain administration and
    management fee on top of the registrar's renewal cost. This covers
    tracking renewal dates, processing the renewal, and keeping the
    domain's settings and records in order. The renewal cost and any fee
    will be shown on your invoice before the renewal is due.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're on an active, paid Website Care Plan, your domain renewal is
    included in your plan and no separate renewal or administration fee
    applies. If you'd rather manage renewals yourself, you can ask us to
    transfer the domain to your own registrar account at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Website Care Plans</h2>
  <p>
    A Website Care Plan is an optional ongoing service agreement that
    keeps your site running after launch. Plans are offered on a monthly
    or annual basis, and the inclusions of your plan will be confirmed in
    writing. A Care Plan may include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting</strong> — keeping your site online on reliable, secure hosting.</li>
    <li><strong>Security updates</strong> — applying updates and fixes to keep your site safe.</li>
    <li><strong>Site backups</strong> — regular backups so your site can be restored if something goes wrong.</li>
    <li><strong>Minor content edits</strong> — small changes to existing text and images, within the limits of your plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Domain renewal management</strong> — your annual domain renewal is handled and covered for you, with no separate renewal or administration fee.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Larger changes, such as new pages or features, fall outside a Care
    Plan and will be quoted separately before any work begins.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Care Plans are billed on a recurring basis — monthly plans on the 1st of every month, and annual plans in advance at the start of each plan year.</li>
    <li>You can cancel a Care Plan by giving us 30 days' written notice. Your plan, and its billing, continues until the end of that notice period.</li>
    <li>If a Care Plan payment isn't made when due, we may suspend hosting, maintenance, and domain management services until the account is brought up to date. We'll contact you before any suspension.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A 50% deposit is payable before work begins.</li>
    <li>The remaining 50% is due on completion, before the site goes live or files are handed over.</li>
    <li>Any ongoing Website Care Plan is billed as set out under Website Care Plans above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we need from you</h2>
  <p>
    To keep your project on track, we need you to provide content (text,
    images, logos) and feedback within a reasonable time when we ask for
    it. Delays on your side may delay the delivery date.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Once your design and build fees have been paid in full, the website
    and, if we registered it on your behalf, its domain name, belong
    entirely to you. Until then,
    the work remains our property. We may keep and display non-confidential
    parts of the finished site in our own portfolio unless you ask us not
    to.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ownership of your website and domain isn't affected by whether you
    have a Care Plan. However, ongoing hosting, maintenance, and domain
    management are services, not part of what you own — they're provided
    only while you have an active service agreement with us (such as a
    Care Plan or domain management arrangement). If that agreement ends,
    we'll help you move your site and domain to a provider of your choice.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel a project at any time by telling us in writing. You'll
    be charged for work already completed up to that point; any deposit
    already paid covering that work is non-refundable, and anything paid
    beyond work actually done will be returned. See our
    <a href={`${base}/refund-policy`}>Refund Policy</a>
    for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We'll do the work with reasonable skill and care, but we can't
    guarantee specific business outcomes (like a particular amount of
    traffic, bookings, or sales) from a website alone. We're not liable
    for losses caused by things outside our reasonable control — for
    example, outages at your hosting provider or a third-party service
    your site depends on. Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or
    modifies any consumer guarantee, right, or remedy you have under the
    Australian Consumer Law that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of New South Wales, Australia,
    and any dispute will be handled in the courts there.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time; the date at the top shows
    when they last changed. Any project already agreed in writing is
    covered by the terms in place when you accepted your quote.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
